            "review_title": "Review at Sin Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Em Happy Travelling Folks\nAustralia13 contributions\n0\nTasty variety\nJul 2025 • Friends\nFirst night in Hanoi, dinner for four adults and four teenagers. Ate upstairs privately. Good food, but delivered staggered. Didn’t eat together really. Drinks limited to beer, wine, coke, water and they weren’t cold (needed to put in ice bucket). Excellent food - tired teenagers loved it! However on departure found out had to pay for peanuts (presented as complimentary on table on arrival), as well as napkins! Didn’t mind, just would’ve preferred we knew from the start. We will ask more people today if this is a cultural practice we just didn’t know about so we are more aware. We ate early as we had been in transit since the day before and they were obliging. Food ranged from mild flavour to quite spicy and all was enjoyed.\nRead more\nWritten July 2, 2025",
            "rating": 5.0,
